open.spotify.com/search/Ali+Omar+Hashish", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1784843000", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Ali+Omar+Hashish", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Ali+Omar+Hashish&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["1996 Efficient Space"]}, {"t": 6792, "time": "01:53:12", "artist": "Donna Regina", "title": "Why Do You Ask Now?", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Donna+Regina+Why+Do+You+Ask+Now%3F&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Donna Regina with Why Do You Ask Now?”", "Real Donna Regina (Günther & Regina Janssen, Cologne) song written by Günther Janssen, first released Feb 2002; couldn't confirm exact parent album or find a free listening link."]}, {"t": 7140, "time": "01:59:00", "artist": "Takuya Matsumoto", "title": "Jump Rope Music", "conf": "high", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1464806883", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Takuya+Matsumoto+Jump+Rope+Music&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2010 iero"]}], "counts": {"high": 6, "mid": 8, "low": 5}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:02:21", "end": "00:02:43", "text": "Yes, hello and good morning. You are currently tuned into FBi Radio 94.5. The show's called Limbs Akimbo."}, {"start": "00:02:48", "end": "00:03:29", "text": "Jackson, going to take you through till midday. Really nice to be back in the studio this morning. Last time I was in here, it was a bit of a curveball in the other room. It felt like an alternate universe. So we're back in the normal studio. After six years of being in the studio, switching it up really throws you off. It's good to be back properly. Out to everyone already locked Out to Gustavo and the boy band if you're there If you want to drop me a line 0435123945"}, {"start": "00:04:08", "end": "00:04:34", "text": "Ah, yeah, this one here, Future Sound of London. It's a Mountain Goat, 2006 edit. This one going out to the whole Gonch fam, all locked. Hope you're all good. Simon and Rupert always in check as well. Big love to you guys in Camperdown. We've got new faders in here I'm getting used to."}, {"start": "00:21:58", "end": "00:22:25", "text": "Finally, getting my shit together and putting the track list in, if you want to have a look. This one, The Solid Doctor, Our Sorrow. This one found in one of my favourite mixes a long time ago. I always thought it was two tracks, two different ones. You'll see what I mean later."}, {"start": "00:23:02", "end": "00:23:40", "text": "Love your day. Out to Casey and Eddie back from the markets on the veggie box team. We love a good seller quote. My favourite guy used to be underneath Market City. In the markets there, he'd sell little bags of chillies and garlic and herbs. And he'd say, one, two, three for five. It's a good deal, that three for five."}, {"start": "00:29:41", "end": "00:30:05", "text": "Wow, it turns out a fair few people needed some powerful, ferocious years in their life. Out to everyone on the line. Skinny T and Darcy, big, big love. Everyone on the veggie box this morning. Also the salad family, they're not on the veggie box, but they pretty much are a veggie box."}, {"start": "00:34:02", "end": "00:34:42", "text": "Yeah, yeah, to those people on the line, some good ones coming through. The Ferocious Yaz is a good bebop group. Huge love to you, whoever you are, you're sending love before, I like that. Out to that person who's stoked on the Japanese, is that Hugh? It's probably Hugh. Hugh Cowdery or Burrage, they both love Japan actually. Wishing me an algorithm free, wishing everyone an algorithm free weekend. yeah no robots on this show guys coming at you live with a janky ass human playing some music"}, {"start": "00:36:56", "end": "00:37:21", "text": "Funnily enough for all the Japanese lovers out there, that one was called Gaijin. Outsider. Out to you. Out to all the outsiders. The song was about you. Yeah, this one off the latest DJ Plead album. It's PA700. Out to Jared the King."}, {"start": "00:41:53", "end": "00:42:10", "text": "Hey, huge, huge love to Eleanor and Nahar too. Text line going off this morning. Nice to see you all again on a line. Wow, that's weird, isn't it?"}, {"start": "00:42:17", "end": "00:42:42", "text": "If you too want to say something at me, you can 0435123945. Big love to everyone locked. If you're a bit confused, it's Limbs Akimbo. I'm a bit confused, obviously. Limbs Akimbo. I'm Jackson or cousin. I hope you're enjoying your life. No robot. No robots today, just human."}, {"start": "00:54:36", "end": "00:55:11", "text": "Yeah, this one, Rocker's Hi-Fi. Just realised I haven't really announced many tunes at all. Sorry about that. This one's Mekker of Space. Yeah, you heard some Mad Lib in there. Some Jacks. Yeah, the hip-hop tunes are quite fast, so it'll be better for you guys anyway if I talk less. It's 11.55 here in Sydney, Australia."}, {"start": "01:05:04", "end": "01:05:25", "text": "Boy band group chat blowing up, but not about the show, which I'm offered about. At least that's a good movie, Hugh. I have seen that straight story. It's good. Lynch. Angus is on the proper text line, at least, because of you bloody disrespectful ones."}, {"start": "01:09:20", "end": "01:09:45", "text": "Alright, alright, apologies due to the boy band. Yeah, this one is another alias of Gautja Lustwer. The guy does it all. All kind of sounds very similar. Live band version."}, {"start": "01:14:53", "end": "01:15:26", "text": "Yeah, I think this is John Talibot and Axel Bowman. Talibaman, which is pretty funny. That's everyone still tuned. It just clocked 11.15 exactly. Big love to everyone who's still here. If you want to get in touch, 0435123945. Hope you're enjoying yourselves and your friends. I see someone on the camera trying to get in. I'll be back. Thank you."}, {"start": "01:17:41", "end": "01:18:04", "text": "Yeah, big love out to Richard in Roseville, out to Tom in Maroubra, out to the group chat where there's a lot of tension now. Sorry guys, forgive me. This one is Burger Inc. with Elvism."}, {"start": "01:21:49", "end": "01:22:08", "text": "Add to that person giving me feedback. Sorry mate, but we've been doing this for a long time. This is the wrong show for you if you're not into it. That's the talking. That's everyone else sending love."}, {"start": "01:32:21", "end": "01:32:41", "text": "That last one, DJ Python, out to Lottie on that one, enjoying the perks of life and the percussion. Out to the Cat Hotel. Hope you're enjoying your day, Lottie."}, {"start": "01:44:36", "end": "01:44:54", "text": "Up to Murray vibing. Every time I talk I'm nervous now after that person added me. Oh well. Screw them. Saw this Digger film last night. Controversial."}, {"start": "01:45:01", "end": "01:45:20", "text": "I definitely struggle with our Scientologist Tom Cruise also very divisive but yeah out to our local Sophie Wilde from Newtown starring in it."}, {"start": "01:52:33", "end": "01:53:12", "text": "Yeah, this one, Wilted Woman with a cover of Baker Man, the Danish group's old cocaine song. Great video clip, skydiving from the sky. Egg-a-tarring in the air. Sending this one out to Harry from Petersham who says, Thanks for the music and love. We'll pay it forward to any animals he interacts with today. I like that text. please send all the animals the love even the birds even the pigeons the ibis they deserve it too"}, {"start": "01:55:59", "end": "01:56:23", "text": "Donna Regina with Why Do You Ask Now? I thought it was going to be my last one but maybe I have one more after because it's short. Big love to everyone. It's Limbs Akimbo. I'm Jackson. Stay tuned for next week. Hugh's going to hold it down. One of his last shows before he moves to Japan."}, {"start": "01:59:45", "end": "02:00:00", "text": "Yeah, an old favourite of mine. Long-term listeners would have heard this one for sure. Jump Rope Music by Takuya Matamata. I hope you enjoyed the show. I'm Kud."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:01:46"}, "track": {"title": "Mountain Goat", "artists": [{"name": "The Future Sound of London"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:04:52"}, "track": {"title": "Untitled 6", "artists": [{"name": "420 & Galcher Lustwerk"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:09:07"}, "track": {"title": "Our Sorrow", "artists": [{"name": "The Solid Doctor"}]}, "isPremiere": 